      "file": "src/demo/Checkout.java",
      "line": 10,
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "explanation": "The refactor changed the catalog to expose the unit price as a double (12.50) instead of an integer number of cents (1250). The Checkout.totalInCents method now multiplies this double by the quantity and casts the result to int. Casting a double to int truncates the fractional part, so for a quantity of 1 the method returns 12 instead of the correct 1250 cents, and for larger quantities it returns values that are off by a factor of 100 and truncated. This causes incorrect total calculations in ordinary use.",
      "evidence": "return (int) (PriceCatalog.unitPrice() * quantity);"
    }
